# Environment configuration

Copy this file to `.env` for local development:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Only variables prefixed with `PUBLIC_` are exposed to the website build. The Studio reads its
RPC endpoint and cluster at runtime from the workspace settings, so it needs no environment
variables beyond the optional defaults below (plus the demo switch).

## Studio

```bash
# Default RPC endpoint shown on the connect screen.
PUBLIC_SOLANA_RPC_URL="https://api.devnet.solana.com"

# Default cluster: mainnet-beta | devnet | testnet | localnet | custom
PUBLIC_SOLANA_CLUSTER="devnet"

# Set to "true" to open the Studio on labeled sample data. Never enable it in production:
# the demo never signs a transaction or contacts an RPC endpoint.
VITE_STUDIO_DEMO="false"
```

## Website (apps/web)

```bash
# Canonical URL used for sitemap and social metadata.
PUBLIC_SITE_URL="https://peridotbase.com"
```

## Notes

- Peridotbase has no server and no database URL. If a value looks like a connection string or a
  secret, it does not belong here.
- Never commit an AI provider key. The assistant accepts keys at runtime and keeps them in
  memory only.
